claude-rag-hook (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * This package has been renamed to hydra-rag-hooks. v0.7.0 is a
    transitional shim that depends on the new package and prints a
    one-line note on install. apt update will pull in
    hydra-rag-hooks automatically; afterwards you can run
    `apt remove claude-rag-hook` to drop this transitional name.
  * The new package supports both Claude Code AND OpenAI's Codex
    CLI from one apt install. Same UserPromptSubmit hook design,
    same retrieval pipeline, same `crh` operator CLI. Existing
    .claude-rag-index/ folders are auto-renamed to .hydra-index/
    on first hook run, with embeddings preserved byte-for-byte.
    Per-user state at ~/.config/claude-rag-hook/ etc. is migrated
    in place to the unified ~/.config/hydra-llm/rag-hooks/ family
    location. No re-indexing, no manual migration steps.
  * See https://ra-yavuz.github.io/hydra-rag-hooks/ for the new
    project's README and changelog.

